      'Following landing — Surface operations and payload activities.',
      'Approximately seven days after landing — NASA payload operations ceased.',
    ],
    verification: 'NASA and the Planetary Data System confirm the launch, landing, location and six NASA payloads. The lander came to rest at an angle; this does not change the classification of the event as a lunar touchdown.',
    lastVerified: VERIFIED_DATE,
    sources: [
      sources.im1Payloads,
      sources.im1Pds,
      sources.im1PressKit,
      sources.im1Launch,
    ],
    payloads: im1Payloads,
  },
  {
    id: 'blue-ghost-1',
    name: 'Blue Ghost Mission 1',
    provider: 'Firefly Aerospace',
    taskOrder: 'TO19D',
    lander: 'Blue Ghost',
    orbitalVehicle: 'None',
    launchVehicle: 'SpaceX Falcon 9',
    launchSite: 'Launch Complex 39A, Kennedy Space Center, Florida, USA',
    launchDate: '15 January 2025',
    launchDateStatus: 'Actual launch date',
    landingDate: '2 March 2025, 08:34 UTC',
    destination: 'Near Mons Latreille, Mare Crisium',
    destinationStatus: 'Actual lunar landing region',
    outcome: 'Successful lunar landing and surface mission. Firefly reported approximately 346 hours of daylight operations and more than five hours of operations into lunar night. Mission operations concluded on 16 March 2025.',
    status: 'Mission concluded',
